    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



(a) Since <m>\displaystyle \sin{(t)} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}</m>, we have <m>t= \pi/4 , (3 \pi)/4</m>.



(b) Since <m>\displaystyle \cos{(t)} = - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}</m>, we have <m>t= (3 \pi)/4 , (5 \pi)/4</m>.



(c) Since <m>\displaystyle \tan{(t)} = - \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}</m>, we have <m>t= (5 \pi)/6 , (11 \pi)/6</m>.



</solution>
